WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:21.659
Magica's royal palace stood in a grand cobblestone square in the exact center of the city, its graceful spires reaching toward the sky.

2
00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:31.261
Normally the square was very crowded. Today, though, only a few people scurried across it, looking this way and that. And none of them were Reds.

3
00:00:31.262 --> 00:00:34.668
Zann and his friends stopped at the edge of the square.

4
00:00:34.669 --> 00:00:38.578
Perda, Gliss, and Darb stared at the palace in awe.

5
00:00:38.579 --> 00:00:44.050
Zann wasn't surprised. There definitely wasn't anything like this in Swamp Bottom!

6
00:00:44.051 --> 00:00:48.075
Just then Darb gasped. "What?" Zann asked.

7
00:00:48.076 --> 00:00:51.109
"Trolls!" Darb whispered, pointing.

8
00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:55.504
Several of the ugly, hulking creatures were lumbering across the square!

9
00:00:55.505 --> 00:01:00.583
The kids all ducked behind some shrubs. "Now what?" Gliss asked.

10
00:01:00.584 --> 00:01:08.390
"We can't just walk up to the palace with those trolls there, even with our disguises. They might recognize us."

11
00:01:08.391 --> 00:01:11.174
"We need a plan," Perda said.

12
00:01:11.175 --> 00:01:16.284
"Yeah," Zann said slowly. "And I think I have an idea."

13
00:01:16.285 --> 00:01:18.714
"What?" Darb asked.

14
00:01:18.715 --> 00:01:25.651
"When I was a little kid, I met a Void named Gert who was an animal caretaker at my parents' lab.

15
00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:31.347
He told me once that there's a secret way to sneak in or out of the palace," Zann said.

16
00:01:31.348 --> 00:01:37.548
"It's an underground tunnel that goes all the way from the palace to a big public park.

17
00:01:37.549 --> 00:01:43.115
Gert said the tunnel was built during the Old Times, when dark magic was everywhere.

18
00:01:43.116 --> 00:01:51.392
The king and queen needed a way to escape in case an enemy struck them with a Dousing spell to keep them from using their magic."

19
00:01:51.393 --> 00:01:56.763
"Really?" Gliss sounded hopeful. "Do you know which park Gert was talking about?"

20
00:01:56.764 --> 00:02:00.845
Zann nodded. "I used to pass it on the way to a friend's house.

21
00:02:00.846 --> 00:02:03.379
We could be there in fifteen minutes."

22
00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:05.356
He led the way through the city.

23
00:02:05.357 --> 00:02:09.044
Like the palace square, all the streets were deserted.

24
00:02:09.045 --> 00:02:12.012
"Where is everyone?" Gliss asked.

25
00:02:12.013 --> 00:02:15.872
"They're probably hiding from those trolls," Perda said.

26
00:02:15.873 --> 00:02:22.165
Soon they reached the park. It was even bigger than Zann remembered, taking up four city blocks.

27
00:02:22.166 --> 00:02:25.707
Dozens of tall stone statues dotted the grounds.

28
00:02:25.708 --> 00:02:32.440
"Wow." Gliss glanced around. "How are we ever going to find a secret tunnel entrance here?"

29
00:02:32.441 --> 00:02:36.983
"Did Gert give you any hints about where to search, Zann?" Perda asked.

30
00:02:36.984 --> 00:02:39.938
"Not that I can remember," Zann said.

31
00:02:39.939 --> 00:02:43.005
"Let's just split up and start looking around."

32
00:02:43.006 --> 00:02:47.194
His friends wandered off and started peering under and around the statues.

33
00:02:47.195 --> 00:02:52.052
Zann kicked at the park's paving stones, testing to see if any seemed loose.

34
00:02:52.053 --> 00:02:58.535
Zing followed Zann around for a while, but then the dragon spotted a buzz worm and started playing with it.

35
00:02:58.536 --> 00:03:02.407
The worm buzzed angrily as Zing tossed it into the air.

36
00:03:02.408 --> 00:03:07.378
"Settle down," Zann told the dragon. "You could help us search, you know."

37
00:03:07.379 --> 00:03:13.348
Zing ignored him, batting the buzz worm under a huge statue of a warrior mounted on a dragon.

38
00:03:13.349 --> 00:03:20.649
Zann sighed. Normally he enjoyed watching Zing play. But today wasn't normal. Not even close.

39
00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:25.787
"See anything?" he called to his friends, who were still checking out the other statues.

40
00:03:25.788 --> 00:03:28.689
Perda had even climbed on top of one.

41
00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:32.356
"Nothing out of the ordinary that I can see," she said.

42
00:03:32.357 --> 00:03:38.172
"We've been searching for half an hour and we're no closer to finding the tunnel entrance," Gliss said.

43
00:03:38.173 --> 00:03:42.403
"Maybe we should go back to the palace. The trolls might have left by now."

44
00:03:42.404 --> 00:03:45.943
Just then Zing let out a squawk of surprise.

45
00:03:45.944 --> 00:03:49.480
"Quit fooling around, Zing!" Zann called.

46
00:03:49.481 --> 00:03:52.657
He bent down and peered under the dragon statue.

47
00:03:52.658 --> 00:03:56.780
"We don't have time for . . ." His voice trailed off. "Zing?"

48
00:03:56.781 --> 00:03:58.916
"What's wrong?" Darb asked.

49
00:03:58.917 --> 00:04:04.306
"He ran under this statue," Zann said. "But now I don't see him."

50
00:04:04.307 --> 00:04:10.373
Then he gasped as Zing's head suddenly popped out from the belly of the stone dragon!

51
00:04:10.374 --> 00:04:14.358
By now Gliss had come over to examine the statue too.

52
00:04:14.359 --> 00:04:17.141
She blinked in surprise when she saw Zing.

53
00:04:17.142 --> 00:04:22.028
"I just checked this one—there was no hole or anything, I swear!

54
00:04:22.029 --> 00:04:25.245
I even felt under it as far as I could reach!"

55
00:04:25.246 --> 00:04:29.545
Zann dropped to his hands and knees and crawled under the stone dragon.

56
00:04:29.546 --> 00:04:34.811
"The hole must be hidden with some kind of a Camouflaging spell," he said.

57
00:04:34.812 --> 00:04:41.437
Zing had disappeared again. Zann pressed his hands against the spot where he'd just seen his dragon.

58
00:04:41.438 --> 00:04:45.377
At first all he felt was smooth, solid stone.

59
00:04:45.378 --> 00:04:51.351
But when he pressed a little harder, the stone dissolved and his hand disappeared into nothingness!

60
00:04:51.352 --> 00:04:56.354
"This is it!" he called, amazed. "We found the secret tunnel!"

61
00:04:56.355 --> 00:05:00.025
He twisted and shoved himself through the invisible hole.

62
00:05:00.026 --> 00:05:05.170
Now that he was inside, he could see that the entire statue was hollow!

63
00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:12.401
Zann glanced toward the back end of the statue just in time to see a spurt of flame coming from that direction.

64
00:05:12.402 --> 00:05:17.642
He crawled toward the flame and saw a narrow tunnel angled steeply downward.

65
00:05:17.643 --> 00:05:23.043
It was pitch-black except for the glow thrown off by Zing's fiery breath.

66
00:05:23.044 --> 00:05:27.361
Darb and the girls had climbed into the statue too.

67
00:05:27.362 --> 00:05:31.851
"Wait up, Zing!" Darb called. "You'll have to be our light."

68
00:05:31.852 --> 00:05:35.851
"Let's stay close together, okay?" Gliss sounded scared.

69
00:05:35.852 --> 00:05:38.751
"I don't want to get lost down here in the dark."

70
00:05:38.752 --> 00:05:41.358
Zann inched his way down the tunnel.

71
00:05:41.359 --> 00:05:47.055
"Whoa!" he cried as he started sliding fast. It was steeper than he'd thought!

72
00:05:47.056 --> 00:05:51.839
He landed on Zing's tail, and the dragon let out an offended squawk.

73
00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:56.103
"Sorry," Zann said. "You should've moved out of the way."

74
00:05:56.104 --> 00:05:59.030
He scooted aside as the others slid down.

75
00:05:59.031 --> 00:06:02.530
"That was a long way down!" Perda exclaimed.

76
00:06:02.531 --> 00:06:05.531
"How will we get back up there without magic?"

77
00:06:05.532 --> 00:06:16.284
"If we make it to the palace, we won't have to worry about that," Zann pointed out. "Come on, let's go."
